# Zimone, Paradox Sculptor: both abilities say "up to two target", so three targets are refused and none at all is allowed. Bot1 has
# Zimone and two Ornithopters. As combat begins on turn 1 the trigger will not take all three, and with no target at all no counter
# is put on anything. On turn 3 the same goes for the {G}{U}, {T} doubling ability: three are refused, none is accepted (it is paid
# for, and taps Zimone, and does nothing), and the turn 3 combat trigger then counters Zimone and one Ornithopter only.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Zimone, Paradox Sculptor
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter#1.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Zimone, Paradox Sculptor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Zimone, Paradox Sculptor; Ornithopter#1; Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Target()
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Zimone, Paradox Sculptor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Zimone, Paradox Sculptor.Activate
! Bot1.Target(Zimone, Paradox Sculptor; Ornithopter#1; Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Zimone, Paradox Sculptor.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Zimone, Paradox Sculptor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Target(Zimone, Paradox Sculptor; Ornithopter#1)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Zimone, Paradox Sculptor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
